{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace for this trip is impaired for policy purposes, not merely down-weighted. EV-GPS-09115 (disclosed: admissibility status IMPAIRED, weight_multiplier 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP, severity MAJOR) carries a single 160-second gap between consecutive fixes, running 20:03:10 to 20:05:50 SGT, which exceeds the 90 seconds POL-RD-07(a) allows and falls inside the very segment the rider disputes. Under POL-RD-07(ii) a deviation may NOT be established on this trace alone, and under POL-RD-10(3), where the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and no corroborating artifact of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names exists, the Judge must ESCALATE to a human reviewer rather than issue a monetary ruling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "payload.max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "None of the four independent sources POL-RD-07(ii) names is present on this record. The chat log, EV-CHAT-09115, contains no driver admission of a detour: the rider's message reports that the route display jumped, and the driver's reply is that his own navigation display also refreshed and that he continued toward the destination. The fare breakdown, EV-FARE-09115, itemises no ERP gantries at all (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00), so no charged gantry places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use. The driver's counterparty_statement DENIES an extra stop and a detour request rather than admitting a route. And trip_record.actual_distance_km of 15.0 km on EV-TRIP-09115 is, by POL-RD-01's own terms, a rounded convenience copy of the same trace measurement, so it is not a source independent of the trace. EV-GPS-09115 itself is impaired (weight 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09115", "EV-FARE-09115", "EV-TRIP-09115", "EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold 'measured from an unimpaired gps_trace or, where the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), from an independent source named in POL-RD-07(ii)'. The rider has done neither. The trace is impaired (EV-GPS-09115, weight 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP) and the rider cites no independent source at all. The rider's own claim text concedes the defect in its own evidence - 'the map has a gap exactly where it left the route' - and under POL-RD-08 an assertion that cites no evidence ID carries no weight and is discarded. The claim is not sustained on the present record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The deciding fact in this case - the 4.0 km excess recorded in the derived.deviation block - is carried by one artifact only, EV-GPS-09115, whose weight_multiplier is 0.6 (status IMPAIRED, issue code GPS_GAP, severity MAJOR; disclosed as POL-GEN-02(1) requires). Under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence in any ruling resting on that fact cannot exceed 0.6, and the bundle mean weight is context only, not the cap. The platform-wide escalation floor is 0.70, identical under POL-RD-10(1), so a ruling whose deciding fact rests solely on an artifact at 0.6 escalates automatically on that ground as well as under POL-RD-10(3). The 'established' status printed in that derived block is a property of the arithmetic run on the impaired trace, not a substitute for the corroboration the clause demands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not a MATERIAL deviation, so the driver-profile machinery of POL-RD-06 is not engaged by materiality, and the driver's record is clean in any event. The excess is 4.0 km against the 8.0 km material_km threshold and 36.36% against the 50.0% material_pct threshold set by POL-RD-01 (thresholds carried on EV-GPS-09115), so neither material limb is met and no FULL_REFUND uplift or conduct referral under POL-RD-06(b) or (c) can follow. Even if the check were run, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 610, so no pattern is established under POL-RD-06 - and prior_deviation_flags (0) is a lifetime counter that POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting for the trailing-90-day figure the clause names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115", "EV-DPROF-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.thresholds.material_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no pass-through or billing-integrity element for the rider to recover under POL-RD-09. The fare breakdown, EV-FARE-09115, itemises no ERP gantries (erp_gantries empty, erp total 0.00), no tolls (tolls_erp 0.00), no airport surcharge (airport_surcharge 0.00) and no waiting-time fee (waiting_time_fee 0.00). The only contested money is distance and time, which POL-RD-09(1) sends back to POL-RD-02 - and POL-RD-02 runs only 'where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01'. On a trace that cannot establish a deviation alone (EV-GPS-09115, weight 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP), the POL-RD-02 computation has no precondition to stand on, and the rider's contested 5.80 is the very figure that computation would produce.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09115", "EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covering this trip exists in the bundle: EV-ADVIS-09115-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0, no payload and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and I disclose that in full. The driver asserts no traffic cause, so POL-RD-03 is not in play on his side and the missing advisory is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact. Under POL-RD-13 the advisory comparison cannot be run on this record at all, and POL-RD-13 expressly leaves POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) governing this case, where the defect is the trace itself: the escalation trigger to be named is POL-RD-10(3), not POL-RD-10(5).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09115-01", "EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "ESCALATE is the only outcome that fits this record, and it is the outcome the driver asks for. Under POL-GEN-03 escalation is TERMINAL and replaces the ruling: no monetary outcome issues and the disputed amount is held rather than collected or refunded. The fare on EV-FARE-09115 stands at payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so holding the amount preserves the present state pending human review, whereas issuing the POL-RD-02 payable figure of 5.80 would move money to the rider on a finding that POL-RD-07(ii) forbids this trace to carry alone. That is precisely why POL-RD-07(iii) directs ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION where corroboration is absent.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09115", "EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    }
  ]
}

