{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this dispute is escalated to a human reviewer under POL-RD-10(3). Escalation is terminal — the disputed SGD 5.80 is held, neither collected from the rider nor refunded to her, and no driver payment is made.\n\nWhy. The GPS trace EV-GPS-09115 contains a single 160-second gap between consecutive fixes, running 20:03:10 to 20:05:50 SGT. That exceeds the 90 seconds POL-RD-07(a) allows, so the trace is impaired for policy purposes, and the gap falls inside the very stretch the rider disputes. On an impaired trace POL-RD-07(ii) forbids establishing a deviation from the trace alone; the excess must be corroborated by one of four independent sources, and this record has none. (1) The chat log is not a driver admission that the vehicle left the route: the rider's 20:08:20 message reports a route-display jump, and the driver's 20:08:50 reply says only that his own navigation display refreshed and that he continued toward the destination — that is not an admission of a detour. (2) The fare breakdown itemises no ERP gantries at all (off-route and on-route ERP 0.00), so no charged gantry places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use. (3) The driver's counterparty statement denies an extra stop and denies a detour request; it does not admit a route. (4) The trip record's actual_distance_km (15.0 km) is, by POL-RD-01's own terms, a rounded convenience copy of the same trace measurement, not a source derived independently of it. With no corroboration, POL-RD-07(iii) and POL-RD-10(3) require escalation rather than a money ruling.\n\nWhat the figures would have shown. The trace distance is 15.0 km against the booked optimal of 11.0 km on EV-TRIP-09115 — an excess of 4.0 km, or 36.4%, above both POL-RD-01 gates (20% and 0.8 km). Reading the gap stretch as a straight line (1.35 km, consistent with the recorded 30 kph) is the reading most favourable to the driver and does not remove the excess. Had a deviation been established, POL-RD-02 on this METERED fare would give recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 11.0 + 0.28 x 22.0) x 1.1 surge, read from the fare breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee = 20.831, and refund = 26.60 charged_total - 20.831 = 5.769, rounded up to 5.80, above the 0.50 de minimis. That arithmetic is correct, but it is not reached: POL-RD-02 runs only on a deviation established under POL-RD-01, and an impaired, uncorroborated trace cannot establish one alone.\n\nOn the missing traffic advisory. EV-ADVIS-09115-01 is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT): no advisory covers this trip. Under POL-RD-13 that makes any traffic excuse weightless under POL-RD-08, and because the driver cites no advisory identifier the absence is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction. The absent advisory is not what escalates this case — the impaired trace is.\n\nConfidence and referral. The fact that drives the escalation — the trace's impairment — is carried by EV-GPS-09115, whose weight_multiplier is 0.6 (status IMPAIRED, issue GPS_GAP). Confidence is therefore capped at 0.6, below the platform's 0.70 floor, which is a second and independent reason the case cannot be decided here (POL-RD-10(1)). No referral issues: the excess is not a MATERIAL deviation (4.0 km is below the 8.0 km threshold and 36.4% below 50%), and there is no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 610 completed trips in 90 days), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged and no driver-conduct referral arises; no charge line is unmatched, so POL-RD-09(4) does not arise.\n\nWhat would resolve it. The raw GPS fixes inside the 20:03:10–20:05:50 window, or any independent source of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names — a driver admission in the chat, a charged gantry on an off-optimal corridor, an admitting counterparty statement, or an independently derived trip distance."
  },
